# 18.8 Structured logging review

External integration logs use bounded fields: `source`, `operation`, `status`, `duration_ms`, `request_attempted`, optional `external_id`, and `error_type` on failure. Physical HTTP metrics remain separate from logical-operation logging, preventing retry double-counting.

Application HTTP logs retain request correlation through `request_id`. Metrics never use request IDs, external IDs, tokens, URLs, or secrets as labels.

